{"chunk_id": "ff2ecc74a991", "text": "This passage closes the violent encounter between Bhima and the Rakshasa Kirmira. Bhima, recalling the Pandavas\u2019 humiliation and conscious of Krishna watching, overwhelms the demon in a brutal wrestling match and kills him, freeing the forest of danger. The narrative then shifts: allies of the Pandavas\u2014Vrishnis, Andhakas, Panchalas, and others\u2014visit them in exile and rage against the injustice done by the Kauravas. Krishna vows that Duryodhana and his allies will fall. Arjuna calms the enraged Krishna by praising his divine nature and recounting his cosmic deeds, identifying him with Vishnu. Finally Draupadi passionately recounts the insults and crimes inflicted on the Pandavas\u2014especially her humiliation in the Kuru court\u2014lamenting that such wrongs remain unavenged. The section intensifies the moral stakes of the exile and foreshadows the coming war.\nAllied kings visit the exiled Pandavas; Krishna vows vengeance, Arjuna praises Krishna\u2019s divine nature, and Draupadi recounts her humiliation and past wrongs by Duryodhana.\nThemes: divine nature of Krishna, exile and alliance, vengeance and justice, Draupadi's humiliation, Pandava-Krishna bond", "vector": [0.0001361324539175257, -0.02890588343143463, -0.01430366188287735, 0.0005937241367064416, -0.02297542802989483, 0.03186432644724846, -0.01728924736380577, -0.009275667369365692, -0.01401867438107729, -0.022324027493596077, 0.015850737690925598, 0.0004940633079968393, 0.005078885704278946, 0.0017964395228773355, -0.012281607836484909, 0.014588650315999985, 0.0431281216442585, -0.016135726124048233, 0.022649727761745453, -0.016868550330400467, 0.0017964395228773355, 0.0038100124802440405, -0.007382535375654697, 0.009275667369365692, -0.016257863491773605, 0.022215459495782852, 0.005000853445380926, -0.02839019149541855, 0.01954200491309166, -0.013659047894179821, -0.019528435543179512, 0.011216296814382076, 0.009689577855169773, 0.003319766139611602, 